---
title: Devices
description: How a user's devices are registered, synced, and revoked across the NeoWorks ecosystem.
---

A NeoWorks account can be active on many devices at once. Each device holds the keys needed
to decrypt the user's [media](/docs/neoworks/storage) and stays in sync through real-time events.

## Registration

When a user signs in on a new device, it completes the OAuth flow and registers a device
record — name, platform, and a public key. The account owner can see every registered device.

## Sync

Changes fan out to a user's devices over NATS JetStream in near real time, so an edit on one
device appears on the others without polling.

## Revocation

A user can revoke any device from their account. Revocation invalidates that device's tokens
and removes its access to encrypted media immediately.

```http
DELETE /devices/:id
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

## Querying devices

Device records are part of the [queryable data layer](/docs/neoworks/openschema), reachable with the
appropriate scope.

